  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "The Israeli political landscape remains in flux following the election of a new Knesset speaker who is an ally of opposition leader Gadi Eisenkot. This appointment, secured with support from the Arab bloc, was described by analysts as a setback for Benjamin Netanyahu's political influence. Following this, Gadi Eisenkot has intensified efforts to form a government, engaging in discussions with Netanyahu's Likud party. Gadi Eisenkot holds a mandate to establish a coalition by December 6, a period that could be extended by an additional 14 days if necessary. Amid these political negotiations, Gadi Eisenkot has publicly addressed regional instability, condemning recent arson attacks in the occupied West Bank and characterising the incidents as acts of Jewish terrorism. Israeli authorities have launched an investigation into these arson events.",
